      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Positive quadratic statistics of zero differences are evaluable when their Fourier support lies inside the explicit-formula band. Entire majorants use this band to bound interval pair counts, while a tunable correlation kernel and symmetric local second differences use related positive energy to bound one linear zero Fourier mode; the targets and optimizers remain distinct.",
