      "proposed_content": "Hardy's phase rotation turns critical-line zeros into real sign geometry, so certified sign changes give a lower bound for line zeros. An independent rectangle or argument-principle count supplies the total; equality of the two counts excludes off-line zeros only inside the certified region.",
