      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_90d81caefd090cb0cefac570c94ac567d7344d0faff069556f4da8fc78043d91",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A prime-number-theorem contour argument consumes the zero-free boundary as a height-dependent allowable shift and optimizes height against truncation and logarithmic-derivative costs. Thus competing explicit regions should be compared as envelopes over the actual height range, because downstream error inherits the usable width function rather than an isolated constant.",
