    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b7c2cd5fcd0e4a78cb2484cf98f5a873df158a455f9788cc6995a2b9ce89cd1e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Leading normalized fractional zero ordinates may be equidistributed while a lower-order Fourier bias survives precisely at frequencies resonant with logarithms of prime powers. Replacing zeta's von Mangoldt weights by Selberg-class coefficients preserves that selection rule, locating the mechanism in Euler-product support rather than zeta-specific notation.",
