    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c5e4458efb17801d7c010b13783d4d0d5accd6a1b4a36b01aea4e952db4937ec",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A complete, error-certified finite zero census can enter later analysis as a bounded lemma: enumerated low zeros may be subtracted from a global reciprocal-square bound, while a uniform counting theorem controls the remote tail. Separately, a continuation-style zero-free scheme can use each certified finite exclusion as the precondition for the next analytic region.",
